to be used with Nanite,

162
00:06:57.839 --> 00:06:58.660
but they are highly recommended

163
00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:01.230
because then you're gonna be able to control,

164
00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:02.910
especially if your world is huge,

165
00:07:02.910 --> 00:07:04.410
you're gonna be able to control

166
00:07:04.410 --> 00:07:07.990
that virtual texturing works just like you get

167
00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:10.750
from Nanite where it actually controls

168
00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:12.990
when the high resolution shows up

169
00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:15.009
based on your positioning in the world.

170
00:07:15.009 --> 00:07:16.829
So it's not gonna be trying everything at the same time.

171
00:07:16.829 --> 00:07:18.810
So it's really super efficient.

172
00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:21.410
So you're using Nanite, using virtual texturing,

173
00:07:21.410 --> 00:07:24.350
you're using Lumen and you're using virtual shadow maps.

174
00:07:24.350 --> 00:07:26.329
And all of these can marry together

175
00:07:26.350 --> 00:07:29.519
to give you a better performance overall.

176
00:07:29.519 --> 00:07:32.360
We've also added a fallback target setting

177
00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:34.680
in the Nanite static meshes.

178
00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:36.720
In this menu, it just allows you

