225
00:09:46.740 --> 00:09:50.080
Now let's take a brief look at virtual shadow maps

226
00:09:50.080 --> 00:09:53.799
and what exactly they, what they are.

227
00:09:53.799 --> 00:09:57.289
What they do on what they help with

228
00:09:57.289 --> 00:10:00.049
is they significantly increase shadow resolution

229
00:10:00.049 --> 00:10:02.690
to match highly detailed Nanite geometry.

230
00:10:02.690 --> 00:10:05.509
So this is what I meant by them pairing together nicely.

231
00:10:05.509 --> 00:10:09.029
Unlike shadow maps in the past, what we had for baking,

232
00:10:09.029 --> 00:10:10.730
which are like texture projecting.

233
00:10:10.730 --> 00:10:14.450
So it's like projects that shadow on the surface.

234
00:10:14.450 --> 00:10:16.730
It's plausible soft shadows

235
00:10:16.730 --> 00:10:20.210
with reasonable controllable performance costs

236
00:10:20.210 --> 00:10:24.610
and provide a simple solution that works for default

237
00:10:24.610 --> 00:10:27.289
with limited amounts of adjustments needed.

238
00:10:27.289 --> 00:10:31.250
So it is now the default when you open up Unreal.

239
00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:33.889
Now you still need to work with some settings and Lumen,

240
00:10:33.889 --> 00:10:35.929
double checking if you're gonna work with them together,

241
00:10:35.929 --> 00:10:37.850
make sure you're using hardware ray tracing

242
00:10:37.850 --> 00:10:39.649
like we talked about before.

243
00:10:39.649 --> 00:10:41.409
And you're gonna replace,

244
00:10:41.409 --> 00:10:44.049
what it does, it also replaces many stationary lights

245
00:10:44.049 --> 00:10:46.330
in the old school baking method,

246
00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:49.509
shadowing technique with a single unified path.

247
00:10:49.509 --> 00:10:51.769
So it makes it so it's a little bit managed,

248
00:10:51.769 --> 00:10:56.110
a lot better managed, manageable in my humble opinion.

249
00:10:56.110 --> 00:10:58.129
And I think it's really great to use.

250
00:10:58.129 --> 00:11:00.529
It's simple, you get up and running quickly

251
00:11:00.649 --> 00:11:03.759
and you can get some really nice visuals.

252
00:11:03.759 --> 00:11:06.000
So made for Lumen mainly,

253
00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:08.279
not intended for Unreal standard baking,

254
00:11:08.279 --> 00:11:12.460
virtual shadow maps is strictly for the Lumen workflows.

255
00:11:12.460 --> 00:11:13.799
If you wanna switch to baking,

256
00:11:13.799 --> 00:11:16.519
you must change your shadow settings in the project

